; lang.xon -- what this bundle is.
;
; xon: read with the ordinary reader and never evaluated, like every manifest
; in the x-lang world (pin.xon, engine.pin.xon). An unknown form is a loud
; error, never a silent skip.
;
; FORMAT (one form per line):
;   (lang "NAME")               the -l name
;   (dialect NAME)              he | xe | rn -- a requirement
;   (requires-release "TAG")    the x-lang this bundle was built against
;   (requires-lang "NAME" ["V"]) another lang this one is written on top
;                               of, optionally at an exact version
;   (entry "FILE")              loaded AFTER the dialect, not instead of it

(lang "sweet")

; Helium: the reader types are plain closures over the catalog's `type`, `buf`
; and `io` prims, all provided by x-core. Nothing here needs a float, a socket,
; or a file.
(dialect he)

; The x-lang release this bundle is built and tested against; CI compares it
; for equality. v0.7.0 or later is required: sweet/ws.x imports
; x/reader/indent, the shared indentation stack, which exists in no earlier
; release.

(requires-release "v0.13.0")

(entry "run.x")
